1
00:00:01,007 --> 00:00:02,847
( birds chirping )

2
00:00:05,267 --> 00:00:07,477
( Kirito groaning )

3
00:00:23,777 --> 00:00:25,447
WHAT THE HELL?

4
00:00:26,577 --> 00:00:27,907
WHERE AM I?

5
00:00:29,407 --> 00:00:31,667
I REMEMBER BEING
AT AGIL’S PLACE.

6
00:00:34,667 --> 00:00:36,457
THEN I LEFT WITH ASUNA.

7
00:00:38,127 --> 00:00:40,677
BUT I CAN’T REMEMBER
WHAT HAPPENED NEXT.

8
00:00:41,757 --> 00:00:42,717
( gasps )

9
00:00:44,427 --> 00:00:45,807
HUH?

10
00:00:46,927 --> 00:00:48,887
MY CLOTHES.

11
00:00:48,887 --> 00:00:51,227
AM I IN A GAME RIGHT NOW?

12
00:00:53,727 --> 00:00:55,067
COMMAND.

13
00:00:56,527 --> 00:00:57,937
LOG OUT?

14
00:01:02,447 --> 00:01:03,867
HUH?

15
00:01:06,157 --> 00:01:08,867
WAY TOO REALISTIC
TO BE A 3-D OBJECT,

16
00:01:08,867 --> 00:01:11,207
SO THIS AIN’T A GAME.

17
00:01:12,577 --> 00:01:15,787
AM I DREAMING? WAIT.

18
00:01:15,787 --> 00:01:18,547
THAT’S IT.
THIS IS THE UNDERWORLD.

19
00:01:18,547 --> 00:01:20,917
I’M HOOKED UP TO THE S.T.L.

20
00:01:20,917 --> 00:01:24,757
BUT THAT CAN’T BE RIGHT.
IF I’M DIVING IN THE S.T.L.,

21
00:01:24,757 --> 00:01:27,927
MY MEMORIES OF THE REAL WORLD
SHOULD BE BLOCKED,

22
00:01:27,927 --> 00:01:29,387
AND I CAN STILL REMEMBER

23
00:01:29,387 --> 00:01:31,387
HANGING OUT
WITH ASUNA AND SINON.

24
00:01:32,767 --> 00:01:35,607
KIKUOKA! HIGA?

25
00:01:35,607 --> 00:01:38,227
ANYONE! ABORT THE DIVE!

26
00:01:38,227 --> 00:01:41,107
I THINK THERE’S
SOMETHING WRONG IN HERE!

27
00:01:46,407 --> 00:01:47,327
( sighs )

28
00:01:49,697 --> 00:01:51,907
( gulping )

29
00:01:51,907 --> 00:01:54,287
THIS IS TOO REAL FOR V.R.

30
00:01:54,287 --> 00:01:55,957
- ( ax chops )
- ( water splashes )

31
00:01:57,497 --> 00:01:59,667
( ax chops )

32
00:01:59,667 --> 00:02:02,377
♪

33
00:02:02,377 --> 00:02:04,257
( gasps )

34
00:02:09,887 --> 00:02:11,637
WHAT WAS THAT?

35
00:02:11,637 --> 00:02:15,977
I DON’T KNOW WHY,
BUT IT FELT SO NOSTALGIC

36
00:02:15,977 --> 00:02:18,017
AND FRUSTRATING.

37
00:02:18,017 --> 00:02:19,937
♪

38
00:02:33,827 --> 00:02:35,207
( singing in Japanese )

39
00:02:41,457 --> 00:02:42,547
♪ WHOA, OH OH ♪

40
00:02:42,547 --> 00:02:44,167
♪ WHOA OH, OH, OH OH OH ♪

41
00:03:02,437 --> 00:03:04,067
♪ DO YOU BELIEVE YOURSELF? ♪

42
00:03:04,067 --> 00:03:07,067
( singing in Japanese )

43
00:03:13,697 --> 00:03:15,997
♪ SHINY SWORD, MY DIAMOND ♪

44
00:03:15,997 --> 00:03:17,867
( singing in Japanese )

45
00:03:29,507 --> 00:03:30,507
♪ IT’S TIME ♪

46
00:03:30,507 --> 00:03:32,427
( singing in Japanese )

47
00:03:48,027 --> 00:03:49,947
( birds chirping )

48
00:03:52,027 --> 00:03:54,117
( ax rings )

49
00:04:02,997 --> 00:04:05,087
( Kirito gasps )

50
00:04:05,087 --> 00:04:06,837
♪

51
00:04:19,807 --> 00:04:20,847
( gasps )

52
00:04:25,027 --> 00:04:26,227
Eugeo: HMM?

53
00:04:26,227 --> 00:04:27,607
( Kirito stammers )

54
00:04:36,997 --> 00:04:38,247
Eugeo: WHO ARE YOU?

55
00:04:38,247 --> 00:04:40,327
ARE YOU FROM AROUND HERE?

56
00:04:40,327 --> 00:04:44,337
Kirito: IS HE A TESTER LIKE ME,
OR IS HE AN NPC?

57
00:04:47,167 --> 00:04:48,877
Eugeo: DO YOU HAVE A NAME?

58
00:04:50,257 --> 00:04:51,257
Kirito: UM...

59
00:04:51,257 --> 00:04:52,887
YEAH, I GOT ONE.

60
00:04:55,097 --> 00:04:57,017
IT’S KIRITO.

61
00:04:57,017 --> 00:04:58,597
Eugeo: KIRITO?

62
00:04:58,597 --> 00:05:00,637
Kirito: I CAME
FROM THE FOREST OVER THERE,

63
00:05:00,637 --> 00:05:03,057
BUT I’M NOT SURE
WHERE I AM OR ANYTHING.

64
00:05:03,057 --> 00:05:05,897
Eugeo: THE FOREST.
OH. YOU MEAN FROM THE SOUTH?

65
00:05:05,897 --> 00:05:08,277
DID YOU WALK
ALL THE WAY FROM ZAKKARIA?

66
00:05:08,277 --> 00:05:10,607
Kirito: NO, I DON’T THINK SO.

67
00:05:10,607 --> 00:05:12,947
I MEAN, IT’S LIKE--

68
00:05:12,947 --> 00:05:16,077
I DON’T KNOW HOW I GOT HERE.
I CAN’T REMEMBER.

69
00:05:16,077 --> 00:05:18,117
Eugeo: WHAT?
THEN, WHERE DO YOU LIVE?

70
00:05:18,117 --> 00:05:20,367
CAN YOU REMEMBER
THE NAME OF THE TOWN?

71
00:05:20,367 --> 00:05:22,867
Kirito: UM, NO.
EVERYTHING’S A BLANK.

72
00:05:22,867 --> 00:05:25,167
I WOKE UP,
AND I WAS IN THE FOREST.

73
00:05:25,167 --> 00:05:27,627
Eugeo: I HEARD THE STORIES,
BUT I NEVER THOUGHT

74
00:05:27,627 --> 00:05:30,087
I’D MEET A REAL, LIVE
LOST CHILD OF VECTA.

75
00:05:30,087 --> 00:05:31,167
I CAN’T BELIEVE IT.

76
00:05:31,167 --> 00:05:33,797
Kirito: HUH? WHAT’S A VECTA?

77
00:05:33,797 --> 00:05:36,047
Eugeo: WAIT. ISN’T THAT
WHAT THEY’RE CALLED

78
00:05:36,047 --> 00:05:37,257
WHERE YOU’RE FROM?

79
00:05:37,257 --> 00:05:39,887
WHEN SOMEONE
DISAPPEARS FROM A VILLAGE,

80
00:05:39,887 --> 00:05:42,887
THEN SUDDENLY TURNS UP
IN A FOREST OR A FIELD,

81
00:05:42,887 --> 00:05:45,477
THAT’S WHAT THEY’RE CALLED,
A CHILD OF VECTA.

82
00:05:45,477 --> 00:05:48,187
THE DARK GOD VECTA
LIKES TO PRANK HUMANS

83
00:05:48,187 --> 00:05:50,857
BY SNATCHING THEM UP,
STEALING THEIR MEMORIES,

84
00:05:50,857 --> 00:05:52,737
AND PLOPPING THEM DOWN
SOMEWHERE FAR FROM HOME.

85
00:05:52,737 --> 00:05:54,277
Kirito: OHH.

86
00:05:54,277 --> 00:05:57,157
I GUESS THAT MUST HAVE BEEN
WHAT HAPPENED TO ME, THEN.

87
00:05:59,287 --> 00:06:02,617
HIS RESPONSES ARE
WAY TOO NATURAL FOR AN NPC.

88
00:06:02,617 --> 00:06:04,537
I’LL TRY THE DIRECT APPROACH.

89
00:06:04,537 --> 00:06:08,087
ANYWAY, I’M KIND OF STUCK, SO...

90
00:06:09,917 --> 00:06:11,877
I WANNA LEAVE.

91
00:06:11,877 --> 00:06:13,757
Eugeo: UH...

92
00:06:13,757 --> 00:06:15,007
HMM.

93
00:06:15,007 --> 00:06:16,717
YES, I’M SURE YOU DO.

94
00:06:20,467 --> 00:06:22,427
I THINK I KNOW HOW TO HELP YOU.

95
00:06:22,427 --> 00:06:25,017
THE FOREST IS HUGE AND
EASY TO GET LOST IN, THOUGH.

96
00:06:25,017 --> 00:06:27,057
I CAN SHOW YOU A PATH
THAT LEADS NORTH.

97
00:06:27,057 --> 00:06:29,067
- AS LONG AS YOU STICK TO IT...
- Kirito: UM, NO.

98
00:06:29,067 --> 00:06:30,727
- Eugeo: YOU WON’T--
- Kirito: SORRY.

99
00:06:30,727 --> 00:06:31,817
I WANNA LOG OUT NOW!

100
00:06:33,447 --> 00:06:36,107
Eugeo: "LOG OUT"?
WHAT DOES THAT MEAN?

101
00:06:36,107 --> 00:06:37,697
Kirito: DAMN IT.

102
00:06:39,827 --> 00:06:41,407
IT’S SLANG, YOU KNOW?

103
00:06:41,407 --> 00:06:43,537
IT’S LIKE A FASTER WAY
OF SAYING,

104
00:06:43,537 --> 00:06:45,367
"I NEED TO FIND
A PLACE TO STAY."

105
00:06:45,367 --> 00:06:48,037
Eugeo: REALLY?
I NEVER HEARD THAT ONE BEFORE.

106
00:06:48,037 --> 00:06:49,287
( Kirito chuckles )

107
00:06:49,287 --> 00:06:50,877
NOW WHAT?

108
00:06:50,877 --> 00:06:53,547
HE COULD BE A TESTER,
BUT IF HE IS,

109
00:06:53,547 --> 00:06:56,007
HIS MEMORIES
ARE DEFINITELY BLOCKED.

110
00:06:56,007 --> 00:06:57,467
Eugeo:
MY VILLAGE IS CALLED RULID,

111
00:06:57,467 --> 00:06:59,177
AND IT’S BEYOND THOSE TREES.

112
00:06:59,177 --> 00:07:01,387
BUT WE DON’T GET MANY TRAVELERS,
SO THERE’S NO INN.

113
00:07:01,387 --> 00:07:03,977
I THINK IF WE GO TO THE CHURCH

114
00:07:03,977 --> 00:07:06,307
AND EXPLAIN YOUR SITUATION
TO SISTER AZALIA,

115
00:07:06,307 --> 00:07:08,307
SHE MIGHT AGREE TO PUT YOU UP.

116
00:07:08,307 --> 00:07:09,897
Kirito: OH. OKAY, THEN.

117
00:07:09,897 --> 00:07:12,397
I’LL GO TO YOUR VILLAGE
AND TALK TO HER.

118
00:07:12,397 --> 00:07:14,147
Eugeo: WAIT A MOMENT!

119
00:07:14,147 --> 00:07:15,607
Kirito: HUH?

120
00:07:15,607 --> 00:07:17,527
Eugeo: YOU’RE A STRANGER
IN THESE PARTS.

121
00:07:17,527 --> 00:07:19,317
I DON’T THINK
THE GUARDS AT THE GATE

122
00:07:19,317 --> 00:07:21,367
ARE GOING TO LET YOU IN
SO EASILY.

123
00:07:21,367 --> 00:07:23,237
HUH. YOU KNOW WHAT?

124
00:07:23,237 --> 00:07:25,827
IF I GO WITH YOU AND TALK
TO THEM, THEY SHOULD UNDERSTAND.

125
00:07:25,827 --> 00:07:27,077
Kirito: THAT’D BE GREAT
IF YOU DID.

126
00:07:27,077 --> 00:07:28,077
THANKS A LOT.

127
00:07:28,077 --> 00:07:30,167
Eugeo: HMM.

128
00:07:30,167 --> 00:07:34,087
BUT I CAN’T GO YET.
I HAVE TO FINISH MY WORK FIRST,

129
00:07:34,087 --> 00:07:37,127
AND I WON’T BE DONE
FOR ANOTHER FOUR HOURS.

130
00:07:37,127 --> 00:07:39,507
Kirito: I DON’T MIND.
I CAN WAIT.

131
00:07:39,507 --> 00:07:41,967
THAT IS, AS LONG
AS IT’S OKAY WITH YOU.

132
00:07:41,967 --> 00:07:44,057
Eugeo: OF COURSE!
HAVE A SEAT ANYWHERE YOU LIKE,

133
00:07:44,057 --> 00:07:45,427
AND I’LL GET TO WORK.

134
00:07:45,427 --> 00:07:47,887
OH. I HAVEN’T TOLD YOU
MY NAME, HAVE I?

135
00:07:47,887 --> 00:07:49,147
Kirito: N-NO.

136
00:07:49,147 --> 00:07:51,727
♪

137
00:07:51,727 --> 00:07:53,357
Eugeo: MY NAME IS EUGEO.

138
00:07:53,357 --> 00:07:54,397
HOW DO YOU DO?

139
00:07:54,397 --> 00:07:55,857
Kirito: EUGEO?

140
00:07:55,857 --> 00:07:58,527
SOUNDS FAMILIAR.

141
00:07:58,527 --> 00:08:00,067
Eugeo: WHAT’S WRONG, SIR KIRITO?

142
00:08:00,067 --> 00:08:02,777
Kirito: UH...

143
00:08:02,777 --> 00:08:03,787
( sighs )

144
00:08:03,787 --> 00:08:05,497
NOTHING.

145
00:08:05,497 --> 00:08:08,367
OH, AND YOU CAN
JUST CALL ME KIRITO.

146
00:08:08,367 --> 00:08:11,667
Eugeo: OKAY. NICE TO MAKE
YOUR ACQUAINTANCE, KIRITO.

147
00:08:14,917 --> 00:08:16,757
- THAT’S RIGHT!
- Kirito: HUH?

148
00:08:16,757 --> 00:08:19,217
Eugeo: YOU MUST BE HUNGRY.

149
00:08:19,217 --> 00:08:20,797
Kirito: OH, THANKS A LOT.

150
00:08:22,177 --> 00:08:24,637
HE’S DEFINITELY NOT AN NPC.

151
00:08:24,637 --> 00:08:28,057
STILL NOT SURE IF HE’S
A TEST PLAYER, THOUGH.

152
00:08:28,057 --> 00:08:30,307
OR MAYBE THIS ISN’T V.R.

153
00:08:30,307 --> 00:08:33,107
MAYBE THIS IS REAL.

154
00:08:33,107 --> 00:08:35,107
Eugeo: THE ONLY GOOD THING
ABOUT THIS BREAD

155
00:08:35,107 --> 00:08:38,607
IS IT KEEPS FOR A LONG TIME,
BUT JUST TO BE SAFE...

156
00:08:41,197 --> 00:08:42,907
( Kirito gasps )

157
00:08:42,907 --> 00:08:47,117
OKAY. LET ME TRY THAT.

158
00:08:47,117 --> 00:08:48,197
( gasps )

159
00:08:48,197 --> 00:08:49,867
THAT SETTLES IT.

160
00:08:49,867 --> 00:08:53,327
THIS AIN’T REALITY
OR A PARALLEL DIMENSION.

161
00:08:53,327 --> 00:08:55,457
IT’S V.R.

162
00:08:55,457 --> 00:08:57,047
- Eugeo: HEY, KIRITO.
- Kirito: WHAT?

163
00:08:57,047 --> 00:09:00,427
Eugeo: DID YOU FORGET HOW TO USE
THE STACIA WINDOW, TOO?

164
00:09:00,427 --> 00:09:02,137
Kirito: NO, ’COURSE NOT.

165
00:09:06,057 --> 00:09:08,217
Eugeo: YOU CAN TAKE YOUR TIME
EATING IT IF YOU WANT.

166
00:09:08,217 --> 00:09:11,347
IT STILL HAS
PLENTY OF LIFE LEFT.

167
00:09:11,347 --> 00:09:13,057
IF THIS WERE SUMMER,

168
00:09:13,057 --> 00:09:14,557
YOU CAN BET IT WOULDN’T
KEEP NEARLY AS LONG.

169
00:09:15,937 --> 00:09:17,397
Kirito: MM.

170
00:09:17,397 --> 00:09:18,857
( groans )

171
00:09:18,857 --> 00:09:19,937
HOLY...

172
00:09:19,937 --> 00:09:22,107
( groans )

173
00:09:22,107 --> 00:09:24,277
Eugeo: IT’S NOT VERY GOOD, HUH?

174
00:09:24,277 --> 00:09:27,037
I GET THEM FROM THE BAKERY
EVERY MORNING ON MY WAY HERE,

175
00:09:27,037 --> 00:09:29,577
BUT IT’S SO EARLY,
THEY ONLY HAVE DAY-OLD BREAD.

176
00:09:29,577 --> 00:09:32,287
AND I DON’T HAVE TIME TO GO BACK
AT NOON FOR FRESH ONES.

177
00:09:32,287 --> 00:09:35,167
Kirito: THAT SUCKS.
DO YOU HAVE TIME TO MAKE LUNCH

178
00:09:35,167 --> 00:09:36,247
OR HAVE SOMEONE ELSE MAKE IT?

179
00:09:36,247 --> 00:09:38,207
( Eugeo gasps )

180
00:09:38,207 --> 00:09:40,007
WELL, ACTUALLY,

181
00:09:40,007 --> 00:09:42,217
SOMEONE USED TO BRING ME
MY LUNCH EVERY DAY,

182
00:09:42,217 --> 00:09:44,087
BUT THAT WAS YEARS AGO.

183
00:09:44,087 --> 00:09:45,087
OH, WELL.

184
00:09:46,677 --> 00:09:47,807
Kirito: SO WHY’D THEY STOP?

185
00:09:49,267 --> 00:09:51,887
♪

186
00:09:51,887 --> 00:09:54,347
Eugeo: SHE WAS
MY CHILDHOOD FRIEND.

187
00:09:54,347 --> 00:09:57,317
SHE WAS THE SAME AGE AS ME.

188
00:09:57,317 --> 00:10:01,317
WHEN WE WERE LITTLE,
WE PLAYED TOGETHER ALL THE TIME.

189
00:10:01,317 --> 00:10:03,987
AND AFTER I RECEIVED MY CALLING,

190
00:10:03,987 --> 00:10:07,157
SHE WOULD BRING ME LUNCH
EVERY DAY WITHOUT FAIL.

191
00:10:07,157 --> 00:10:08,407
BUT THEN...

192
00:10:09,487 --> 00:10:11,247
BECAUSE OF ME...

193
00:10:11,247 --> 00:10:14,287
THE TWO OF US WENT
TO EXPLORE A CAVE UP NORTH,

194
00:10:14,287 --> 00:10:15,957
AND BY ACCIDENT,

195
00:10:15,957 --> 00:10:18,417
SHE CROSSED THE BOUNDARY
INTO THE DARK TERRITORY,

196
00:10:18,417 --> 00:10:21,627
A PLACE NO HUMAN
IS ALLOWED TO ENTER, EVER.

197
00:10:21,627 --> 00:10:23,967
THE TABOO INDEX FORBIDS IT.

198
00:10:23,967 --> 00:10:25,837
Kirito: TABOO INDEX?

199
00:10:26,967 --> 00:10:28,257
Eugeo: THE NEXT DAY,

200
00:10:28,257 --> 00:10:30,307
AN INTEGRITY KNIGHT
CAME TO OUR VILLAGE...

201
00:10:31,977 --> 00:10:34,727
AND HE TOOK HER TO CENTORIA
TO BE EXECUTED.

202
00:10:37,687 --> 00:10:41,187
BUT I STILL BELIEVE
SHE’S ALIVE, KIRITO.

203
00:10:41,187 --> 00:10:42,357
I KNOW IT.

204
00:10:42,357 --> 00:10:44,527
SOMEWHERE IN CENTORIA,

205
00:10:44,527 --> 00:10:46,357
ALICE IS ALIVE.

206
00:10:46,357 --> 00:10:48,447
Kirito: ALICE.

207
00:10:48,447 --> 00:10:50,237
I KNOW THAT NAME.

208
00:10:52,247 --> 00:10:54,827
ALICE.

209
00:10:54,827 --> 00:10:56,747
- Eugeo: I’M SORRY.
- ( Kirito gasps )

210
00:10:56,747 --> 00:10:59,287
Eugeo: I DIDN’T MEAN
TO DUMP ALL THAT ON YOU.

211
00:10:59,287 --> 00:11:00,837
I KNOW WE JUST MET AND ALL,

212
00:11:00,837 --> 00:11:03,127
BUT IT FEELS
LIKE WE’RE OLD FRIENDS.

213
00:11:03,127 --> 00:11:06,127
Kirito: OH, THAT’S OKAY.
I DON’T MIND.

214
00:11:06,127 --> 00:11:08,547
SO WHY DON’T YOU GO FIND HER?

215
00:11:08,547 --> 00:11:12,217
GO TO CENTORIA OR WHEREVER,
SEE IF SHE’S THERE?

216
00:11:12,217 --> 00:11:14,977
Eugeo: EVEN IF I HAD
THE FASTEST HORSE IN THE LAND,

217
00:11:14,977 --> 00:11:17,687
IT WOULD TAKE A WEEK
TO GET THERE FROM HERE.

218
00:11:17,687 --> 00:11:20,647
Kirito: THEN THROW SOME CLOTHES
AND FOOD IN A BAG AND WALK.

219
00:11:20,647 --> 00:11:23,357
Eugeo: IF I COULD
DO THAT, I WOULD,

220
00:11:23,357 --> 00:11:26,237
BUT I CAN’T
JUST ABANDON MY CALLING.

221
00:11:26,237 --> 00:11:29,407
THE TABOO INDEX FORBIDS IT.
YOU KNOW THAT.

222
00:11:29,407 --> 00:11:32,157
Kirito: OH, RIGHT.
YOU GOT A POINT.

223
00:11:32,157 --> 00:11:33,237
UM...

224
00:11:34,367 --> 00:11:36,407
SORRY TO BE NOSY,

225
00:11:36,407 --> 00:11:39,997
BUT ABOUT HOW LONG AGO
DID ALL THIS HAPPEN, ANYWAY?

226
00:11:39,997 --> 00:11:43,377
Eugeo: IT WAS MY 11th SUMMER,
SIX YEARS AGO.

227
00:11:43,377 --> 00:11:44,627
WANT SOME WATER?

228
00:11:44,627 --> 00:11:45,837
( Kirito gasps )

229
00:11:48,047 --> 00:11:49,967
THANKS. MAYBE LATER.

230
00:11:49,967 --> 00:11:51,547
( Eugeo chuckles )
WELL, LUNCH IS OVER,

231
00:11:51,547 --> 00:11:53,137
SO I BETTER GET BACK TO WORK.

232
00:11:53,137 --> 00:11:55,307
I STILL HAVE TO MEET
MY QUOTA FOR TODAY.

233
00:11:55,307 --> 00:11:57,727
Kirito: I’LL JUST KICK BACK
’TIL YOU FINISH, THEN.

234
00:11:57,727 --> 00:12:00,477
BY THE WAY, YOUR CALLING,
WHAT IS IT?

235
00:12:00,477 --> 00:12:01,437
Eugeo: YOU’LL SEE.

236
00:12:01,437 --> 00:12:03,267
IT’S NOT VERY EXCITING.

237
00:12:08,487 --> 00:12:10,867
( ax chops )

238
00:12:13,447 --> 00:12:14,827
( ax rings )

239
00:12:16,197 --> 00:12:18,287
( Eugeo sighs )

240
00:12:24,337 --> 00:12:26,377
( sighs )

241
00:12:26,377 --> 00:12:28,587
Kirito: SO, LIKE, YOUR CALLING’S
TO CHOP DOWN TREES?

242
00:12:28,587 --> 00:12:30,387
Eugeo: YEAH.

243
00:12:30,387 --> 00:12:32,717
OFFICIALLY, MY TITLE’S
SUPPOSED TO BE WOODCUTTER.

244
00:12:32,717 --> 00:12:35,387
THE PROBLEM IS, I HAVEN’T
CUT A SINGLE TREE DOWN

245
00:12:35,387 --> 00:12:37,557
IN THE SEVEN YEARS
SINCE I RECEIVED MY CALLING.

246
00:12:37,557 --> 00:12:39,097
Kirito: WHAT?

247
00:12:39,097 --> 00:12:40,727
Eugeo: MY JOB’S
TO WORK ON THIS TREE.

248
00:12:40,727 --> 00:12:42,357
IT’S CALLED THE GIGAS CEDAR.

249
00:12:42,357 --> 00:12:44,147
THE VILLAGERS CALL IT
SOMETHING ELSE, THOUGH...

250
00:12:45,527 --> 00:12:47,487
"THE DEMON TREE."

251
00:12:47,487 --> 00:12:49,397
THEY CALL IT THAT,
BECAUSE IT SUCKS UP

252
00:12:49,397 --> 00:12:52,447
ALL OF TERRARIA’S BLESSINGS
FROM THE LAND AROUND IT.

253
00:12:52,447 --> 00:12:55,327
RULID HAS ALWAYS WANTED
TO PLANT MORE WHEAT FIELDS,

254
00:12:55,327 --> 00:12:58,367
BUT AS LONG AS THIS IS HERE,
NOTHING GOOD WILL GROW.

255
00:12:58,367 --> 00:13:00,117
THE VILLAGE
HAD THAT DRAGONBONE AX

256
00:13:00,117 --> 00:13:02,327
SENT FROM THE CAPITAL
AND APPOINTED A WOODCUTTER

257
00:13:02,327 --> 00:13:05,167
TO WORK ON IT EVERY DAY
’TIL THE TREE CAME DOWN.

258
00:13:05,167 --> 00:13:06,877
THAT’S MY JOB.

259
00:13:06,877 --> 00:13:09,467
Kirito: SO FOR
THE PAST SEVEN YEARS NOW,

260
00:13:09,467 --> 00:13:11,507
YOU’VE BEEN
CHOPPING AWAY AT IT?

261
00:13:11,507 --> 00:13:15,047
AFTER ALL THAT TIME,
THAT’S AS FAR AS YOU GOT?

262
00:13:15,047 --> 00:13:16,927
- ( Eugeo chuckles ) HARDLY.
- Kirito: EH?

263
00:13:16,927 --> 00:13:19,767
Eugeo: I’M ACTUALLY
A SEVENTH-GENERATION WOODCUTTER.

264
00:13:19,767 --> 00:13:21,387
THAT’S OUR CALLING.

265
00:13:21,387 --> 00:13:23,017
SOMEONE’S BEEN
CHOPPING AWAY ON IT

266
00:13:23,017 --> 00:13:26,107
EVERY SINGLE DAY
FOR 300 YEARS, IN FACT.

267
00:13:26,107 --> 00:13:28,067
Kirito: F-FOR 300 YEARS?!

268
00:13:32,407 --> 00:13:33,357
HEY, EUGEO...

269
00:13:34,737 --> 00:13:36,447
MIND IF I TAKE A CRACK AT IT?

270
00:13:36,447 --> 00:13:38,697
Eugeo: HUH?!

271
00:13:38,697 --> 00:13:41,657
Kirito: I MEAN, YOU DID GIVE ME
HALF YOUR LUNCH, DIDN’T YOU?

272
00:13:41,657 --> 00:13:44,497
SO IT’S ONLY FAIR I SHOULD
PICK UP HALF YOUR WORK.

273
00:13:44,497 --> 00:13:46,457
Eugeo: OH, I DON’T KNOW. I MEAN,

274
00:13:46,457 --> 00:13:49,297
THE TABOO INDEX DOESN’T SAY
I CAN’T HAVE SOMEONE HELP,

275
00:13:49,297 --> 00:13:51,417
EVEN THOUGH IT IS
MY CALLING AND ALL.

276
00:13:51,417 --> 00:13:54,757
TRY IT, BUT IT’S
MUCH HARDER THAN IT LOOKS.

277
00:13:54,757 --> 00:13:57,217
Kirito: I WON’T KNOW ’TIL I TRY.

278
00:13:57,217 --> 00:13:58,097
HERE GOES NOTHIN’.

279
00:14:00,177 --> 00:14:03,017
♪

280
00:14:11,237 --> 00:14:14,487
( yells )

281
00:14:14,487 --> 00:14:15,447
( groans )

282
00:14:17,237 --> 00:14:20,157
- ( wincing )
- ( Eugeo laughing )

283
00:14:20,157 --> 00:14:21,827
Kirito: YOU DON’T
HAVE TO LAUGH THAT HARD.

284
00:14:21,827 --> 00:14:24,037
Eugeo: I’M SORRY ABOUT THAT.

285
00:14:24,037 --> 00:14:27,247
YOU PUT WAY TOO MUCH TENSION
INTO YOUR SHOULDERS AND HIPS.

286
00:14:27,247 --> 00:14:29,957
RELAX, AND LET THE MOMENTUM
DO THE WORK FOR YOU.

287
00:14:33,417 --> 00:14:36,467
Kirito: THAT’S RIGHT.
THIS IS A VIRTUAL WORLD.

288
00:14:36,467 --> 00:14:40,387
IT’S NOT ABOUT MY REAL ABILITY,
BUT MY AVATAR’S.

289
00:14:40,387 --> 00:14:42,057
♪

290
00:14:44,807 --> 00:14:46,517
( breathes deeply )

291
00:14:46,517 --> 00:14:49,477
SWORD SKILL, SMASH!

292
00:14:49,477 --> 00:14:50,567
( yells )

293
00:14:59,527 --> 00:15:00,867
( sighs )

294
00:15:00,867 --> 00:15:02,747
Eugeo: WHOA,
THAT WAS A NICE HIT!

295
00:15:02,747 --> 00:15:06,417
GO ON. GIVE IT ANOTHER SHOT,
BEFORE YOU FORGET.

296
00:15:07,497 --> 00:15:08,497
Kirito: 50!

297
00:15:08,497 --> 00:15:09,537
( ax chops )

298
00:15:09,537 --> 00:15:11,337
( sighs )

299
00:15:11,337 --> 00:15:14,217
Eugeo: OKAY,
THAT’S 1,000 STRIKES.

300
00:15:14,217 --> 00:15:17,087
Kirito: REALLY?
WE DID THAT MANY TODAY?

301
00:15:17,087 --> 00:15:20,927
Eugeo: UH-HUH. 500 FOR ME,
AND 500 FOR YOU.

302
00:15:20,927 --> 00:15:22,677
ADD THE 1,000
I DID THIS MORNING,

303
00:15:22,677 --> 00:15:24,597
AND THAT’S 2,000 STRIKES TOTAL.

304
00:15:24,597 --> 00:15:26,687
THAT’S THE DAILY QUOTA
FOR MY CALLING.

305
00:15:26,687 --> 00:15:27,687
( Kirito laughs )

306
00:15:27,687 --> 00:15:29,517
( thinking ) OH, MY GOD.

307
00:15:29,517 --> 00:15:31,647
Eugeo: YOU’RE A NATURAL
AT THIS, KIRITO.

308
00:15:31,647 --> 00:15:34,237
THANKS TO YOUR SKILL,
I HAD AN EASY DAY TODAY.

309
00:15:34,237 --> 00:15:36,317
Kirito: I DON’T KNOW ABOUT THAT.

310
00:15:36,317 --> 00:15:38,907
I BET YOU WOULD HAVE
HAD IT CUT IT DOWN BY NOW

311
00:15:38,907 --> 00:15:40,447
IF I WASN’T HERE
MESSING AROUND.

312
00:15:40,447 --> 00:15:42,537
Eugeo: UH...

313
00:15:42,537 --> 00:15:45,657
THINK SO?
THEN YOU NEED TO SEE SOMETHING.

314
00:15:45,657 --> 00:15:47,617
( Kirito gasps )

315
00:15:47,617 --> 00:15:51,337
Eugeo: IT’S ONLY GONE DOWN
BY ABOUT 50 SINCE LAST MONTH.

316
00:15:51,337 --> 00:15:53,297
THAT’S NORMAL, ACTUALLY.

317
00:15:53,297 --> 00:15:55,047
IT’S A STRONG TREE.

318
00:15:55,047 --> 00:15:57,547
SO WHAT IF WE DIDN’T MAKE
A LOT OF PROGRESS TODAY?

319
00:15:57,547 --> 00:15:58,927
IN THE END,
IT DOESN’T REALLY MAKE

320
00:15:58,927 --> 00:16:00,547
MUCH OF A DIFFERENCE AT ALL.

321
00:16:00,547 --> 00:16:01,597
( chuckles )

322
00:16:01,597 --> 00:16:03,137
LET’S GO.

323
00:16:05,467 --> 00:16:07,437
Kirito: WAIT.
YOU FORGOT TO LOCK IT.

324
00:16:07,437 --> 00:16:08,437
Eugeo: WHAT FOR?

325
00:16:08,437 --> 00:16:09,687
Kirito: WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

326
00:16:09,687 --> 00:16:11,397
SOMEONE COULD STEAL IT.

327
00:16:11,397 --> 00:16:12,897
Eugeo: NOW, WHO’D DO THAT?

328
00:16:12,897 --> 00:16:15,027
IT CLEARLY STATES
IN THE TABOO INDEX

329
00:16:15,027 --> 00:16:16,857
THAT THEFT
IS FORBIDDEN, REMEMBER?

330
00:16:16,857 --> 00:16:18,607
Kirito: OH. YEAH, THAT’S RIGHT.

331
00:16:18,607 --> 00:16:20,737
Eugeo: COME ON.
I’LL SHOW YOU MY VILLAGE.

332
00:16:20,737 --> 00:16:21,987
Kirito: UM, BUT--

333
00:16:23,327 --> 00:16:24,697
HEY, WAIT UP!

334
00:16:26,617 --> 00:16:28,537
♪

335
00:16:41,257 --> 00:16:42,677
HUH?

336
00:16:42,677 --> 00:16:43,757
Guard: HEY, EUGEO.

337
00:16:45,387 --> 00:16:46,847
WHO’S YOUR NEW FRIEND?

338
00:16:46,847 --> 00:16:48,597
Eugeo: HEY, ZINK.

339
00:16:48,597 --> 00:16:51,057
THIS IS KIRITO.

340
00:16:51,057 --> 00:16:53,647
I THINK HE’S
A LOST CHILD OF VECTA.

341
00:16:54,767 --> 00:16:56,147
Zink: THAT TRUE?

342
00:16:56,147 --> 00:16:57,737
YOU CAN’T REMEMBER ANYTHING?

343
00:16:57,737 --> 00:16:59,397
Kirito: UM, NO?

344
00:16:59,397 --> 00:17:01,357
Zink: DID YOU FORGET
YOUR CALLING, TOO?

345
00:17:01,357 --> 00:17:02,697
Kirito: YEAH, I GUESS.

346
00:17:02,697 --> 00:17:04,197
Zink: HMPH.

347
00:17:04,197 --> 00:17:07,117
IT WAS PROBABLY
A LOUSY CALLING, ANYWAY.

348
00:17:07,117 --> 00:17:09,907
BET IT WAS
AS LAME AS EUGEO’S HERE.

349
00:17:09,907 --> 00:17:11,957
HE’S GOT ONE
OF THE MOST POINTLESS CALLINGS

350
00:17:11,957 --> 00:17:13,497
IN ALL THE LAND!

351
00:17:14,997 --> 00:17:17,207
NOW, MINE, I’M A MAN-AT ARMS,

352
00:17:17,207 --> 00:17:18,837
- AND LET ME TELL--
- Kirito: SWORDSMAN.

353
00:17:18,837 --> 00:17:21,797
THAT’S MY CALLING, MAN.
I’M A SWORDSMAN.

354
00:17:21,797 --> 00:17:23,717
Zink: A SWORDSMAN?

355
00:17:23,717 --> 00:17:26,427
A SCRAWNY, WEAK-LOOKIN’
PIPSQUEAK LIKE YOU?

356
00:17:26,427 --> 00:17:28,017
YOU CAN’T EVEN LIFT A SWORD.

357
00:17:28,017 --> 00:17:30,057
HMPH.

358
00:17:32,477 --> 00:17:35,817
GO ON, THEN.
SHOW US YOUR "SKILL."

359
00:17:35,817 --> 00:17:36,767
( Kirito chuckles )

360
00:17:41,067 --> 00:17:43,527
LET’S SEE HOW I DO WITH THIS.

361
00:17:43,527 --> 00:17:45,197
♪

362
00:17:47,737 --> 00:17:50,077
( Eugeo stammering )

363
00:17:52,747 --> 00:17:54,327
( Kirito yells )

364
00:18:00,337 --> 00:18:01,717
( both gasp )

365
00:18:01,717 --> 00:18:03,377
Kirito: NO WAY.

366
00:18:05,757 --> 00:18:08,347
THAT WAS A LIGHT EFFECT.

367
00:18:08,347 --> 00:18:10,467
THERE’S SWORD SKILLS HERE.

368
00:18:10,467 --> 00:18:13,057
Eugeo: THAT WAS AMAZING!

369
00:18:13,057 --> 00:18:15,937
I DIDN’T KNOW
YOU HAD SKILLS LIKE THAT!

370
00:18:15,937 --> 00:18:18,477
MAYBE YOU WERE A SENTINEL
IN SOME BIG CITY.

371
00:18:18,477 --> 00:18:20,687
Kirito: I-I DON’T KNOW, MAYBE.

372
00:18:20,687 --> 00:18:22,187
- Eugeo: ZINK?
- ( Zink gasps )

373
00:18:22,187 --> 00:18:23,897
Eugeo: WILL YOU LET KIRITO IN?

374
00:18:23,897 --> 00:18:26,237
I’D LIKE TO SHOW HIM
AROUND THE VILLAGE NOW.

375
00:18:27,617 --> 00:18:29,287
♪

376
00:18:35,787 --> 00:18:37,037
Kirito: I’M TIRED.

377
00:18:37,037 --> 00:18:38,747
Eugeo: WELL, WE’RE HERE.

378
00:18:38,747 --> 00:18:40,087
Kirito: FINALLY.

379
00:18:40,087 --> 00:18:43,127
IS THIS REALLY OKAY? I MEAN,

380
00:18:43,127 --> 00:18:46,547
EVERYONE’S JUST GONNA ACCEPT I’M
ONE OF THOSE LOST VECTA KIDS?

381
00:18:46,547 --> 00:18:48,507
Eugeo: ISN’T THAT WHAT YOU ARE?

382
00:18:48,507 --> 00:18:51,097
Kirito: YEAH. I GUESS SO.

383
00:18:51,097 --> 00:18:54,187
Eugeo: LET’S TALK TO THE SISTER
AND GET YOU SORTED OUT.

384
00:19:01,647 --> 00:19:02,397
( door opens )

385
00:19:04,027 --> 00:19:05,737
Azalia: WHAT DO YOU BOYS WANT?

386
00:19:05,737 --> 00:19:09,077
Kirito: UH, I...

387
00:19:09,077 --> 00:19:10,617
Sister: HMM?

388
00:19:10,617 --> 00:19:11,787
( gasps )

389
00:19:11,787 --> 00:19:13,037
( Eugeo gasps )

390
00:19:13,037 --> 00:19:14,787
( sighs )

391
00:19:14,787 --> 00:19:17,747
Sister: HERE. I BROUGHT YOU
A PILLOW AND A BLANKET.

392
00:19:17,747 --> 00:19:20,997
PRAYERS BEGIN AT 6:00.
BREAKFAST IS AT 7:00.

393
00:19:20,997 --> 00:19:22,837
I’LL COME CHECK ON YOU,

394
00:19:22,837 --> 00:19:24,717
BUT PLEASE TRY
TO GET UP ON TIME.

395
00:19:24,717 --> 00:19:26,757
DO NOT BE LATE FOR PRAYERS.

396
00:19:26,757 --> 00:19:29,677
YOU DO NOT WANT
TO MAKE SISTER AZALIA MAD.

397
00:19:29,677 --> 00:19:32,887
ALSO, WE HAVE A CURFEW
AFTER LIGHTS-OUT, SO MIND THAT.

398
00:19:32,887 --> 00:19:34,057
( girl gasps ) SHE SAW US!

399
00:19:34,057 --> 00:19:35,637
- Boy: RUN!
- ( sister sighs )

400
00:19:35,637 --> 00:19:37,227
HONESTLY.

401
00:19:37,227 --> 00:19:39,357
NOW THEN, DO YOU
HAVE ANY QUESTIONS?

402
00:19:39,357 --> 00:19:41,937
Kirito: NO, I’M GOOD.
THANKS FOR SETTING ME UP.

403
00:19:41,937 --> 00:19:42,937
( sister sighs )

404
00:19:42,937 --> 00:19:45,947
WELL, GOOD NIGHT, THEN.

405
00:19:45,947 --> 00:19:48,027
YOU KNOW HOW TO PUT OUT
THE LAMP, RIGHT?

406
00:19:48,027 --> 00:19:49,067
Kirito: YEAH.

407
00:19:49,067 --> 00:19:50,867
GOOD NIGHT, SELKA.

408
00:19:52,027 --> 00:19:53,197
( Selka grunts )

409
00:20:00,627 --> 00:20:02,037
( Kirito sighs )

410
00:20:03,667 --> 00:20:05,837
THIS AIN’T THE REAL WORLD,

411
00:20:05,837 --> 00:20:10,217
AND AS FAR AS I CAN TELL,
NONE OF THE VILLAGERS ARE NPCs.

412
00:20:10,217 --> 00:20:12,427
BUT THEY CAN’T
BE TESTERS, EITHER.

413
00:20:12,427 --> 00:20:14,097
THERE’D HAVE TO BE
DOZENS OF S.T.L.s

414
00:20:14,097 --> 00:20:15,517
FOR THEM TO LOG IN WITH,

415
00:20:15,517 --> 00:20:17,557
AND I KNOW
THERE AREN’T THAT MANY.

416
00:20:17,557 --> 00:20:20,147
WHAT’D EUGEO SAY?

417
00:20:20,147 --> 00:20:22,517
( no audible dialogue )

418
00:20:22,517 --> 00:20:24,437
ACCORDING TO HIM,

419
00:20:24,437 --> 00:20:27,237
MORE THAN 300 YEARS
HAVE PASSED IN THIS WORLD.

420
00:20:27,237 --> 00:20:29,857
HE’S SPENT THE LAST SIX
AS A WOODCUTTER HERE

421
00:20:29,857 --> 00:20:33,197
AND REMEMBERS
HIS CHILDHOOD HERE, TOO.

422
00:20:33,197 --> 00:20:36,077
IF THAT’S TRUE,
THEN HIM AND THE OTHERS...

423
00:20:40,747 --> 00:20:41,957
HMM? ( gasps )

424
00:20:43,087 --> 00:20:44,667
OH.

425
00:20:49,877 --> 00:20:53,217
EUGEO AND THE VILLAGERS
WERE RAISED HERE FROM THE START,

426
00:20:53,217 --> 00:20:55,557
BUT THE ONLY WAY
THAT COULD HAPPEN

427
00:20:55,557 --> 00:20:58,227
IS IF RATH COPIED
THE SOULS OF BABIES.

428
00:20:58,227 --> 00:21:00,637
BABIES...

429
00:21:00,637 --> 00:21:03,187
ARTIFICIAL FLUCTLIGHTS.

430
00:21:03,187 --> 00:21:06,107
IT’S HARD TO BELIEVE, BUT
THERE’S NO OTHER EXPLANATION.

431
00:21:06,107 --> 00:21:08,687
BUT WHY WOULD RATH DO THAT?

432
00:21:08,687 --> 00:21:11,027
AND HOW FAST WOULD THEY
HAVE TO ACCELERATE TIME

433
00:21:11,027 --> 00:21:12,527
TO GET THIS WORLD TO THIS POINT?

434
00:21:15,617 --> 00:21:17,947
AND WHAT IF I’M
STUCK HERE FOREVER

435
00:21:17,947 --> 00:21:19,457
AND NEVER GET BACK HOME?

436
00:21:22,117 --> 00:21:24,077
MAYBE I CAN
GET IN TOUCH WITH KIKUOKA

437
00:21:24,077 --> 00:21:26,497
IF I GET TO A BIGGER CITY.

438
00:21:26,497 --> 00:21:30,047
I NEED MONEY TO TRAVEL,
AND, RIGHT NOW, I GOT NONE,

439
00:21:30,047 --> 00:21:32,587
AND I DON’T KNOW ENOUGH
ABOUT THIS WORLD YET.

440
00:21:34,927 --> 00:21:39,177
IF I HAD SOME HELP,
I COULD GET TO CENTORIA

441
00:21:39,177 --> 00:21:41,727
AND FIND SOME ANSWERS THERE.

442
00:21:41,727 --> 00:21:43,687
♪

443
00:21:43,687 --> 00:21:45,357
( woman vocalizing )

444
00:22:04,997 --> 00:22:06,247
♪

445
00:22:42,327 --> 00:22:46,167
♪ THE IRIS TO YOU ♪

446
00:23:36,167 --> 00:23:38,417
NEXT TIME: THE END MOUNTAINS

